second will overwrite the first. This is deliberate: re-running an analysis
usually means replacing this morning's figure, not accumulating a dozen
copies of it. Set \code{hms = TRUE} when you want every run kept.

Both stamps come from a single \code{\link[=Sys.time]{Sys.time()}} call, so a run that straddles
midnight cannot emit a date and a time from opposite sides of it.

The extension is whatever \code{\link[tools:file_ext]{tools::file_ext()}} considers it, which is only
the final component: \code{data.tar.gz} becomes \verb{data.tar_2026-08-10.gz}. A file
name with no extension gets the stamp appended at the end.

