None of them takes any further arguments — a shorthand you have to pass
toggles to is not shorter. For the time-only case, call \code{dated_path()}
directly.

Note that \code{dp()} is deliberately \emph{not} \code{dated_path()} with its defaults:
the full name defaults to printing, the two-letter forms do not. Inline in
a busy call the quiet version is usually what you want, and the \code{p} is
there to ask for the record when you do.
